---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../components/TrustBar.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import Needed from '../components/Needed.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/site.js';
import { client } from '../data/client.js';

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: client.owner.name,
  jobTitle: client.owner.role,
  worksFor: { '@id': `${client.url}/#business` },
};
---
<Layout
  path="/about/"
  title="About Swift Electrical & Security"
  description="Swift Electrical & Security is run by Adil, a NICEIC registered electrician working across Bradford and West Yorkshire. Electrical work and security systems from the same person."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
  schemas={[personSchema]}
>
  <Hero inner={true}>
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Electrics and security, from the same person.</h1>
    <p class="hero__sub">
      Swift Electrical &amp; Security is run by Adil, working across Bradford and
      West Yorkshire.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <div class="container"><TrustBar /></div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="frame reveal">
        <Placeholder
          src={client.owner.photo}
          alt={`${client.owner.name}, ${client.name}`}
          label="Photo of Adil needed"
          hint="Real photo, not stock. There are 18 posts on the Instagram already — a still from one of those would do to start."
          variant="ph--portrait"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2>Adil</h2>
        <p class="lead">{client.owner.bio}</p>
        <p class="muted">
          Three of the seven reviews on the Google profile name him. One
          describes him driving forty minutes out of his way to sort a lighting
          fault. Another describes being talked through exactly what needed
          doing before anything was done. A third, from a landlord with several
          properties, says his was the most reasonable of every quote received.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          The security side is not an add-on. It is in the name, and two of the
          seven reviews are about camera installs, one of them from a customer who
          has used the company several times.
        </p>
        <div class="ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;padding:24px;margin-top:22px;text-align:left">
          <strong>Adil's own words needed here</strong>
          <small>
            How he got into the trade, what he did before, why he added security
            to the electrical side. Two or three paragraphs, first person, in
            his voice. This is the highest-trust content on the site.
          </small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--panel">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head reveal">
        <h2>What the badge actually means</h2>
        <p>
          Awareness of the competent-person schemes has been measured at around
          14%, so most people have no idea what NICEIC registration involves.
          This is what it buys you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="creds">
        <div class="cred reveal">
          <span class="cred__ico"><Icon name="shield" /></span>
          <h3>NICEIC registered</h3>
          <p>
            An independent assessor inspects the work every year. It also means
            we self-certify to Building Control, so you get the compliance
            certificate your solicitor asks for when you sell.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:12px"><Needed label="ENROLMENT NUMBER — so you can check the register" /></p>
        </div>

        <div class="cred reveal" style="transition-delay:80ms">
          <span class="cred__ico"><Icon name="clipboard" /></span>
          <h3>Certified and notified</h3>
          <p>
            We test to BS 7671 and certify the work. Notifiable jobs, meaning new
            circuits, board changes and anything in a bathroom, go to Building
            Control instead of being skipped.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cred reveal" style="transition-delay:160ms">
          <span class="cred__ico"><Icon name="check" /></span>
          <h3>Qualifications</h3>
          <p>The tickets behind the work, listed so you can see them rather than take them on trust.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:12px"><Needed label="2391? 18th Edition? ECS card?" /></p>
        </div>

        <div class="cred reveal" style="transition-delay:240ms">
          <span class="cred__ico"><Icon name="star" /></span>
          <h3>Insured</h3>
          <p>Public liability cover, with the figure stated rather than a vague "fully insured".</p>
          <p style="margin-top:12px"><Needed label="COVER AMOUNT" /></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="inline-cta reveal">
        <p>Want the numbers before you book? Ask and we'll send them over.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--act" href={href('/contact/')}>Ask us <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow reveal">
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>
        Testing and fixing are two different jobs. We keep them that way: you
        get told what we found and what it will cost before anything starts.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        We will not tell you something is urgent when it is not. An old fuse board is worth
        knowing about. It is rarely an emergency, and anyone telling you
        otherwise on your doorstep is selling, not advising.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand title="Want a price?" />
</Layout>

<style>
  li { display: flex; gap: 13px; align-items: flex-start; }
  li svg { width: 20px; height: 20px; color: var(--brand); flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 4px; }
  li strong { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); margin-bottom: 3px; }
  li span { color: var(--muted); }
  li strong { color: var(--text); }
</style>
